  <div class="prose">
    <h3>Update Y</h3>
    <p>The register, the kitchen and the handheld are easier to use on the screens people actually have.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Search on the register shows its filter chips, a result count and suggestions as you type, on desktop, phones and tablets.</li>
      <li>Every page has a shortcut list, and the g shortcuts jump between pages. The 0 key adds the tenth menu item.</li>
      <li>Kitchen tickets keep one fixed size, two rows to a screen. A new "By status" view puts late tickets first, then the ones close to late. When a cook's tap is refused, the screen says why and keeps them signed in.</li>
      <li>Kitchen tickets and receipts print names with curly quotes and the · dot instead of dropping the line.</li>
      <li>Guest receipts no longer print a brand line.</li>
      <li>The handheld for servers, on a landscape tablet, opens items, actions and discounts as a side panel instead of covering the check.</li>
      <li>New side work lists: tasks are added by hand or from a template for each role, and each person sees their own list.</li>
      <li>The time clock shows this week and has a form to ask for a fix to a punch.</li>
      <li>The shift log has its own place in the sidebar.</li>
      <li>The Roles page shows who can view and who can edit checks. Checks stay open to every role that works with orders.</li>
      <li>Fixes: open-check cards stop stretching full width, and dashboard cards in a row line up to the same height.</li>
      <li>Security improvements.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Update X</h3>
    <p>Mostly about working faster at the register and in the kitchen, with a few fixes that stop surprises mid-shift.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Search on the register is smarter: type a category, a tag or a price range like $4-6, and the menu narrows as you type.</li>
      <li>On a keyboard, the register shows its shortcuts after your first key press, and quiet tips in the status line teach the faster way without popping anything up.</li>
      <li>When you add a round to a check that was already sent, the kitchen ticket shows only the new items.</li>
      <li>The kitchen screen is easier to read: it counts finished items, says when a ticket has more lines, labels served items, and shows "All caught up" when the board is clear. Cooks can mark an item done across every ticket from the All Day view.</li>
      <li>New shift log: staff leave handover notes that can name a teammate, and that person can reply. Notes are permanent.</li>
      <li>Closing the day starts with a check that lists anything still open and explains how the expected cash was worked out.</li>
      <li>Staff roles show their permissions grouped into plain areas, and every permission change is recorded.</li>
      <li>The handheld for servers shows "Sent" in its status line instead of covering the screen.</li>
      <li>Fixes: a wrong clock-in PIN no longer signs anyone out; a table frees up only when its last open check closes; a check closed on another device shows as closed.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Earlier updates</h3>
    <p>Ten earlier updates, installed from September 25, laid the groundwork: the register, checks, the kitchen screen, printing, roles and reports.</p>
    <h3>By the numbers</h3>
    <p>Counted by script from the release list and the build stats on 2026-10-10:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>12</strong> updates installed since September 25</li>
      <li><strong>115</strong> new features and <strong>59</strong> fixes since September 23</li>
    </ul>
